Fri Nov 13 16:40:25 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Update to 3.22.0
  * New features:
    + LANG-1790: Add optional FIFO ordering for TimedSemaphore
      blocking acquisitions
  * Fixed Bugs:
    + Include 0x7E (~) in RandomStringUtils nextGraph and nextPrint
    + Default unbounded WildcardType upper bound to Object in
      TypeUtils
    + Take FastDatePrinter era names from the locale's calendar
    + LANG-1655: Preserve Korean text in stripAccents
    + LANG-1835: Ignore synthetic methods in AnnotationUtils
    + LANG-1836: Make TypeUtils.containsTypeVariables and
      unrollVariables honour the owner type of a ParameterizedType
    + Recurse into nested annotation arrays in AnnotationUtils
      .hashCode
    + [javadoc] Correct CharUtils default-value conversion
      descriptions
    + Preserve enclosing context and member names in ClassUtils
      .getShortClassName(Class)
    + Keep RandomUtils's randomDouble() and randomFloat() below the
      exclusive upper bound
    + Use standalone month names for month-only patterns in
      FastDatePrinter
    + Fix TypeUtils.isAssignable rejecting Class<X> to Class<?>
      assignments
    + LANG-1837: Prevent null returns from lazily initialized string
      caches
    + Escape CharSequence values in ToStringStyle.JSON_STYLE
    + LANG-796: Clarify DateUtils calendar arithmetic and daylight
      saving time behavior
    + Treat an unmatched quote as closed in ExtendedMessageFormat
    + Prevent StringUtils padding from splitting surrogate pairs
    + LANG-441: DateUtils Javadoc does not fully define round()
      behavior
    + LANG-1838: Fix resource paths for unnamed packages
    + Keep EventCountCircuitBreaker event count from wrapping on int
      overflow
    + Reject varargs candidates with too few arguments in
      MemberUtils
    + LANG-1323: Align built type hashes with JDK reflection
    + Keep array encoding intact in ClassUtils.getAbbreviatedName
    + Reject leading whitespace in NumberUtils.createNumber
    + Keep StrSubstitutor from treating a value's trailing $ as an
      escape
    + Fix FastDateParser normalization of out-of-range ISO
      day-of-week values
    + [javadoc] Correct StringUtils example methods and overloads
    + Stop ExceptionUtils.removeCommonFrames at the first differing
      frame
    + Use StackTraceElement objects to build compact root cause
      stack traces, avoiding text parsing and preventing exception
      message text from being mistaken for stack frames
    + Restrict LocaleUtils.toLocale to ASCII language, country, and
      numeric area codes; previously accepted non-ASCII codes now
      cause IllegalArgumentException
    + Deprecate ExceptionUtils.removeCommonFrames(), which is now
      used only by tests. Root-cause stack trace generation compares
      StackTraceElement objects directly
    + Keep DateUtils.ceiling and round inside a DST overlap hour
    + Keep RandomStringUtils.random rejection cap from failing valid
      ranges
    + [javadoc] Correct hexadecimal output examples in Conversion
    + Fix Conversion hex method Javadoc
    + Make FastDatePrinter time-zone tests deterministic
    + LANG-1839: Fix recursive toString traversal cleanup
    + LANG-1341: Javadoc: Clarify superclass equality in
      EqualsBuilder
    + LANG-1423: Javadoc: Include wrapping operations in StringUtils
      overview
    + LANG-980: Use enum constants for duration format units in
      DurationFormatUtils
    + LANG-1198: Javadoc: Clarify stripEnd character-set semantics
    + Keep FastDateFormat able to parse the '+hh:mm' offsets its own
      'Z' patterns format
    + Pad BMP code points to four hex digits in UnicodeEscaper
      .toUtf16Escape
  * Changes:
    + Bump org.apache.commons:commons-parent from 105 to 107

