    + Emit surrogate pair for supplementary code points in
      UnicodeEscaper
    + Fix MethodUtils.getMatchingMethod false ambiguity on boxed
      arguments
    + Fold supplementary code points in
      CharSequenceUtils.regionMatches
    + Fix WordUtils.containsAllWords missing words across line
      breaks
    + Handle supplementary code points in WordUtils case methods
    + Fix StringUtils.getDigits dropping supplementary digits
    + Keep StrBuilder.reverse from splitting surrogate pairs
    + Fix NumberUtils min/max varargs dropping the sign of zero
    + Handle supplementary code points in
      StringUtils.splitByCharacterType()
    + LANG-1828: Fix OOM in StringUtils.leftPad/rightPad when size
      is Integer.MIN_VALUE
    + Fix Strings.CI.indexOf() returning out-of-range index for
      empty search
    + LANG-1827: Support escaped single quotes ('') in
      DurationFormatUtils format patterns
    + Keep DurationFormatUtils.lexx() from merging repeated fields
      split by a literal
    + Reject hex letters in NumericEntityUnescaper decimal scan
    + Keep FastDateParser numeric parse from throwing on int
      overflow
    + Keep FastDateParser.parse error message intact for Japanese
      imperial locale
    + Keep ExtendedMessageFormat from rejecting a quoted format
      style
    + Match String case folding in StrBuilder.equalsIgnoreCase
    + Fix FieldUtils.getField false ambiguity on inherited interface
      field
    + Skip Chuvash locale parser tests on Java 27
    + Fix ArrayUtils.reverse range underflow on Integer.MIN_VALUE
      end
    + Fix sign extension in BitField.getValue for top-bit fields
    + Fix int overflow in FluentBitSet.setInclusive at
      Integer.MAX_VALUE
    + Add messages when throwing NullPointerException
    + [Javadoc] Fix Failable class comment to clarify comparison of
      lambda versions
    + LANG-1829: Add tests for DateUtils.truncatedCompareTo and
      truncatedEquals
    + LANG-1830: Avoid repeated regex compilation in ClassUtils
      .toCleanName()
    + Add missing test for ObjectUtils.isEmpty(Object) and
      wait(Object, Duration)
    + Fix negative week year formatting in FastDatePrinter
    + Keep abbreviateMiddle off surrogate pair boundaries
    + LANG-1815: Fix AnnotationUtils.equals for package-private
      annotations
    + Fix two Javadoc errors in StringUtils
    + Reject non-ASCII hex characters in Conversion.hexDigitToInt
    + Fix the overflow bound direction in
      Instants.toMillisSince(Instant)
    + Fix spurious overflow in Fraction.multiplyBy for unreduced
      operands
    + Fix low surrogate false match in StringUtils
      containsAny/containsNone/indexOfAny
    + Keep StringUtils.chop from splitting a trailing surrogate
      pair
    + Keep StringUtils stripStart and stripEnd off surrogate pair
      boundaries
    + Fix the month/day example in DurationFormatUtils.formatPeriod
      Javadoc
    + Fix typos in Javadoc and example comments
    + Fix CharRange.contains(CharRange) for negated argument ranges
    + Fix SpotBugs USO_UNSAFE_METHOD_SYNCHRONIZATION in CharSet
    + Keep StopWatch.formatSplitTime from clamping splits to int
      millis
    + Keep StringUtils left, right, mid, and overlay off surrogate
      pair boundaries
    + Align ReflectionDiffBuilder with AbstractReflection and add
      cycle detection to prevent StackOverflowError on cyclic object
      graphs
    + Fix DurationFormatUtils.formatPeriod() calculation when
      pattern omits 'M'
    + FastDateParser parses 'Y' (week year) as plain calendar year;
      asymmetric with FastDatePrinter and with SimpleDateFormat;
      boundary dates shift by a full year, silently
    + UnicodeUnescaper.unescapeJava/EcmaScript/Json: malformed \u
      sequences throw undeclared IllegalArgumentException, AND
      non-ASCII digit spellings of \u escapes are silently accepted;
      both arms of one missing ASCII-hex prescan
    + StringUtils.replaceEachRepeatedly derives its recursion budget
      from the input itself; the documented StackOverflowError
      protection fails on large tables, and expanding rules amplify
      text 64x even at the default TTL
    + EventUtils.EventBindingInvocationHandler.invoke() dispatches
      Object.hashCode/equals/toString into the bound business method
      (empty-eventTypes default), or returns null -> NPE from hash
      collections (non-empty)
    + LocaleUtils static caches no longer grows on invalid input to
      LocaleUtils.countriesByLanguage(String)
    + LocaleUtils static caches no longer grows on invalid input to
      LocaleUtils.countriesByLanguage(String)
    + ExtendedMessageFormat.applyPattern() is quadratic: full
      pattern.toCharArray() per token
    + WordUtils.wrap(wrapLongWords=false, the 2-arg default) copies
      the entire remaining string every iteration.
    + FastDateParser.parse throws undeclared
      IllegalArgumentException, NullPointerException, and
      IllegalStateException on crafted date strings
    + Memoizer: default caches the first failure forever, has no
      size bound or eviction, and runs the user computation inside
      the ConcurrentHashMap bin lock (blocking unrelated keys,
      deadlocking reentrant use)
    + StringEscapeUtils.escapeEcmaScript() misses
      backtick/template-literal (`, ${) and inline-script
      parser-state sequences (<!--, <script) - claim 'Deals
      correctly with quotes' is falsified by ES6
    + StrSubstitutor (deprecated) recursive expansion has a cycle
      check but no fan-out, depth, or size bound
    + DurationFormatUtils.formatPeriod walks the calendar one year
      per iteration, Long.MAX_VALUE endMillis forces ~292 million
      Calendar round trips on one thread
    + JavaVersion.get() throws NumberFormatException where javadoc
      promises null
    + Match Javadoc to code in SystemProperties.getProperty() and
      SystemUtils.getEnvironmentVariable() and update inline
      comments
    + Fix LockingVisitors Javadoc to match code
    + DoubleRange/Range accept NaN endpoints, silently producing a
      half-unbounded range, contains()/fit() fail open for every
      value above the minimum
    + BitField long-mask fields silently mis-answer int/short/byte
      accessors: shifts masked mod 32, and sign extension makes
      above-bit-31 flags read as set on any negative holder
    + ClassUtils.getClass() name normalization (whitespace stripping
      + dot-to-dollar rewriting) defeats host-side class-name string
      checks
    + Fraction.getFraction(String) throws undeclared
      ArithmeticException on crafted numeric strings
      ('9999999999.5', '1/0', mixed-number overflow)
    + StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml4/3 apostrophe gap: single-quoted
      and unquoted HTML attribute contexts are trivially breakable,
      and the javadoc discloses the gap only as an HTML4
      entity-legality footnote
    + ArrayUtils.addAll/insert length arithmetic overflows
      (undeclared NegativeArraySizeException) while sibling concat
      is overflow-checked
    + FormattableUtils.append pads right-justified output with
      insert(0) per char; O(width^2); '%500000s' costs ~1.25e11 char
      moves
    + Attacker-controlled exception message forges frames in
      getRootCauseStackTrace output AND suppresses all real frames,
      beyond cosmetic log spoofing
    + StrBuilder.indexOf materializes the whole builder as a String
      per call; deleteAll/replaceAll multiply it into ~750 GB churn
      on a 1 MB builder
    + ThresholdCircuitBreaker accepts negative increments and
      overflows its accumulator, silently keeping the breaker closed
    + ExceptionUtils.getThrowableList() cycle check is O(n^2) over
      deep cause chains; all chain-walking consumers inherit it
    + Reflection builders' cycle registry unregisters per-visit:
      cycle-SAFE but DAG-exponential, a 40-level reference diamond
      drives ~2^40 traversals and unbounded output
    + FastDateFormat static caches grow without bound per distinct
      pattern/zone/locale, untrusted patterns pin several KB each,
      forever
    + Fix Fraction.add and subtract for operands not in lowest terms
    + Fix MethodUtils.invokeMethod on instances of non-public
      classes
    + Fraction.add and subtract return the reduced form when an
      operand is zero
    + Return null for out-of-range offset in FastTimeZone
      .getGmtTimeZone
    + Fix TypeUtils.toString() recursion and bound handling on
      recursive generic types
    + LANG-1834: Fix Fraction reduction for Integer.MIN_VALUE
    + Defensively clone the TimeZone in FastDatePrinter and
      FastDateParser
    + Defensively clone time zones used as FastDateFormat cache keys
      to prevent caller mutations from returning formatters with
      stale time zone rules
    + Fix ConstructorUtils.getMatchingAccessibleConstructor on
      non-public classes
    + Fix NumberUtils.createNumber() and isCreatable() for positive
      Long literals with explicit '+' sign
    + Fix StrBuilder.lastIndexOf(String) start index for an empty
      search
    + Fix int overflow in Conversion count and position bounds
      guards
    + Preserve serialization compatibility with 3.20.0 for Range,
      IntegerRange, LongRange, and DoubleRange by retaining Range
      serialVersionUID 1L
      Streams written by 3.21.0 RC1 with UID 2L require reading with
      RC1 and exporting endpoint and comparator values before
      rebuilding ranges with this release
  * Changes:
    + Bump org.apache.commons:commons-parent from 92 to 105
    + [test] Bump org.apache.commons:commons-text from 1.14.0 to
      1.15.0

